# Nothing here is ignored any more.
#
# The model directories used to be, because a session could have read a rival's
# work out of the git object store. Sessions now run in a throwaway directory
# outside the repo and the sandbox denies the repo outright, `.git` included, so
# committing results no longer hands them to anyone. Publishing them is the
# point: the comparison is only useful if people can read it afterwards.
#
# One sequencing rule survives: a session can still reach the network, and the
# remote is public. Collect and push after a batch finishes, never while runs
# are in flight.
